[{:db/id "dd4e95b0-b50d-508f-9ef8-253434a7e666" :answer/id #uuid "dd4e95b0-b50d-508f-9ef8-253434a7e666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{e}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ee820ac2-8d37-51d4-9ed8-671965aed8ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee820ac2-8d37-51d4-9ed8-671965aed8ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["dd4e95b0-b50d-508f-9ef8-253434a7e666"] :answer-field/correct "dd4e95b0-b50d-508f-9ef8-253434a7e666" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "0be68eb4-fee3-576f-ac3a-d663b1b8b84c" :question/id #uuid "0be68eb4-fee3-576f-ac3a-d663b1b8b84c" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=e^{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-1}$ at the point where $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=e^{u},\\,u={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=e^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ & =e^{u}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-4x) \\\\ & =(3{x}^{2}-4x)e^{u} \\\\ & =\\left(3 x^{2} - 4 x\\right) e^{x^{3} - 2 x^{2} - 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|_{x=2} & =(3{x}^{2}-4x)e^{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-1}|_{x=2} \\\\ & =(3(2)^{2}-4(2))e^{(2)^{3}-2(2)^{2}-1} \\\\ & =4\\cdot e^{-1} \\\\ & =\\frac{4}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["ee820ac2-8d37-51d4-9ed8-671965aed8ce"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "232f798f-be1c-5feb-b192-a0aa8f6e1c00" :answer/id #uuid "232f798f-be1c-5feb-b192-a0aa8f6e1c00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 4 e" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8a6accfd-1e78-52a0-aedb-2b24f192df2d" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a6accfd-1e78-52a0-aedb-2b24f192df2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["232f798f-be1c-5feb-b192-a0aa8f6e1c00"] :answer-field/correct "232f798f-be1c-5feb-b192-a0aa8f6e1c00" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3cb5cb4c-646e-54f0-9994-bb70583c546b" :question/id #uuid "3cb5cb4c-646e-54f0-9994-bb70583c546b" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=e^{-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+1}$ at the point where $x=-2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=e^{u},\\,u=-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=e^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ & =e^{u}\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}-4x) \\\\ & =(-3{x}^{2}-4x)e^{u} \\\\ & =\\left(- 3 x^{2} - 4 x\\right) e^{- x^{3} - 2 x^{2} + 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=-2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|_{x=-2} & =(-3{x}^{2}-4x)e^{-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+1}|_{x=-2} \\\\ & =(-3(-2)^{2}-4(-2))e^{-(-2)^{3}-2(-2)^{2}+1} \\\\ & =-4\\cdot e^{1} \\\\ & =- 4 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["8a6accfd-1e78-52a0-aedb-2b24f192df2d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "bf4e16e0-23db-53b1-abb3-c9ad70be10d5" :answer/id #uuid "bf4e16e0-23db-53b1-abb3-c9ad70be10d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{12}{e^{5}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "34988f5d-3257-5d67-92f7-baf90f520a47" :answer-field/id #uuid "34988f5d-3257-5d67-92f7-baf90f520a47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["bf4e16e0-23db-53b1-abb3-c9ad70be10d5"] :answer-field/correct "bf4e16e0-23db-53b1-abb3-c9ad70be10d5" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "07e0afd0-4729-561c-85c0-8bd11d965ce5" :question/id #uuid "07e0afd0-4729-561c-85c0-8bd11d965ce5" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=e^{-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1}$ at the point where $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=e^{u},\\,u=-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=e^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6{x}^{2}+6x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ & =e^{u}\\cdot (-6{x}^{2}+6x) \\\\ & =(-6{x}^{2}+6x)e^{u} \\\\ & =\\left(- 6 x^{2} + 6 x\\right) e^{- 2 x^{3} + 3 x^{2} - 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|_{x=2} & =(-6{x}^{2}+6x)e^{-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1}|_{x=2} \\\\ & =(-6(2)^{2}+6(2))e^{-2(2)^{3}+3(2)^{2}-1} \\\\ & =-12\\cdot e^{-5} \\\\ & =- \\frac{12}{e^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["34988f5d-3257-5d67-92f7-baf90f520a47"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a58cd849-c476-5d2a-aa64-d8b6b04a580d" :answer/id #uuid "a58cd849-c476-5d2a-aa64-d8b6b04a580d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1f0c0cc9-ce45-5282-a4db-796430d6adf7" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f0c0cc9-ce45-5282-a4db-796430d6adf7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["a58cd849-c476-5d2a-aa64-d8b6b04a580d"] :answer-field/correct "a58cd849-c476-5d2a-aa64-d8b6b04a580d" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "50ee9513-e646-50a4-ac90-7dd2ba8b0b7a" :question/id #uuid "50ee9513-e646-50a4-ac90-7dd2ba8b0b7a" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=e^{-{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}+4}$ at the point where $x=-2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=e^{u},\\,u=-{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=e^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4{x}^{3}+6x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ & =e^{u}\\cdot (-4{x}^{3}+6x) \\\\ & =(-4{x}^{3}+6x)e^{u} \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 x^{3} + 6 x\\right) e^{- x^{4} + 3 x^{2} + 4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=-2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|_{x=-2} & =(-4{x}^{3}+6x)e^{-{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}+4}|_{x=-2} \\\\ & =(-4(-2)^{3}+6(-2))e^{-(-2)^{4}+3(-2)^{2}+4} \\\\ & =20\\cdot e^{0} \\\\ & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["1f0c0cc9-ce45-5282-a4db-796430d6adf7"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a4527057-c6d9-5ff2-a509-e0ee92396e73" :answer/id #uuid "a4527057-c6d9-5ff2-a509-e0ee92396e73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{12}{e^{8}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "91d46c5a-53e0-5eb2-af1a-36f86eae2ff0" :answer-field/id #uuid "91d46c5a-53e0-5eb2-af1a-36f86eae2ff0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["a4527057-c6d9-5ff2-a509-e0ee92396e73"] :answer-field/correct "a4527057-c6d9-5ff2-a509-e0ee92396e73" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a9053d53-838d-5e57-a71a-28c1ae22fb94" :question/id #uuid "a9053d53-8